course: dictionary
lesson: 8478
title: Same: not different, or the very one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Same is a small word with several jobs. Most of the time it means not different: just like the other one. «Dodging a question isn't the same as lying» tells you the two things do not match, even though they might look alike.
explain: Same can also mean one and the very one, not another. «We go to the same school» means one particular school. When you see «at the same time», read the words around it: it means together, at one moment, and it can also mean «but also».
explain: Same changes its job depending on the sentence. As an adverb, «in the same way» means in a matching way. In maths, «the same number in each» group means equal groups, so you might multiply or divide.
explain: Talk changes too. Friends say «Same!» to mean «me too», and the exam voice might say «identical» instead. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have the right one.
fact: Same means not different: just like the other one.
fact: «The same as» compares two things that match, or shows that they do not.
fact: «At the same time» means together, at one moment, or «but also».
fact: «Same!» or «same here» is casual talk for «me too».
fact: In maths, shapes that are the same size and shape are called congruent. Other formal words for same include identical and equivalent.
exercise: «Dodging a question isn't the same as lying.» In this sentence, what does «the same as» show? | It says a question is a kind of lie | *It says the two things are not alike | It means very quietly | It says the two things are exactly equal
exercise: «The sneaky pair sound exactly the same, "ay".» What does the same mean here? | *Identical, sounding just alike | Loud and happy | Wrong and muddled | Different and far apart
exercise: «Old diving bells kept people dry under water the same way.» What does «the same way» mean? | Under the water only | In a different way | *In a similar, matching way | Very quickly
test: «We go to the same school.» What does same mean here? | Hungry and late | Like a bird | Not different, just like the other one | *One and the very one, not another
test: Which phrase means together, at one moment? | the same as | *at the same time | same old, same old | in the same way
exam: In the exam voice, which word means the same and exactly alike? | famished | *identical | sneaky | glum
